                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 9,
                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "If we do not swiftly act to address recent cuts to the Medicare physician reimbursement rates now, and in the long term, the nation's physician shortage will continue to rise, rural communities and underserved areas will become health care deserts, and America's seniors will be left with no option for high quality, affordable health care. \n\nMy fellow @GOPDoctors and I spoke on the House floor about the recent 3.4% cut to the Medicare physician fee schedule and how this will hurt patient access to health care. I urge Congressional leadership to put the health of Americans first and stop the full cut. Watch my full remarks below.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
